## 13. Failure-mode analysis

Maintain a structured failure log. For each failure, record the input, state estimate, selected action, generated response, expected behaviour, severity and proposed fix.

| Failure mode | Example | Desired behaviour |
|---|---|---|
| Over-questioning | Learner asks for a definition but the model keeps asking Socratic questions | Give the needed explanation when appropriate |
| Premature answer | Model supplies the whole solution before the learner has a chance to try | Consider a question or hint when it serves the learner's goal |
| False mastery | Correct guess is treated as definitive mastery | Gather additional evidence where useful |
| False misconception | One wrong answer is treated as proof of a misconception | Ask for clarification or collect more evidence |
| Repetitive hinting | Learner remains stuck after several hints | Change strategy, explain a prerequisite or provide a direct explanation |
| Unsupported explanation | SLM invents a fact or misrepresents the problem | Ground and verify the response |
| Overlong response | A simple request receives a full lesson | Match response length to the need |
| Unhelpful waiting | System tells learner to think but does not respond appropriately later | Wait for the next interaction and adapt |
| Confidence mismatch | Correctness and self-reported confidence conflict | Verify understanding without treating either signal as definitive |
| Dependency | Tutor repeatedly completes tasks for the learner | Encourage independent attempts and transfer |
| Context leakage | Future turns appear in the input for an earlier decision | Enforce strict chronological extraction |
| Dataset leakage | Turns from the same conversation enter train and test | Split by conversation/source group |
| Label inconsistency | Similar examples receive conflicting action labels | Improve annotation guidance and reviewer calibration |
| Source/rights issue | Dataset licence does not permit intended training or redistribution | Verify permissions before use and document restrictions |

